A study of the distribution amplitudes for the $ho$, $ho^*$, and $D^*_s$ mesons is conducted using a light-front quark model. These distribution parameters are then used to calculate the S-wave parts of the relevant two-body annihilation form factors and decay widths for the processes $B 	o \pi e  ar{
u}$, $B 	o ho e  ar{
u}$, $B 	o \phi e  ar{
u}$, $B 	o ho(770) \gamma$, $B 	o D^*_s \gamma$, and $B_s 	o \phi(959) \gamma$. The findings show that the $D$ mesons' distribution amplitudes exhibit axial symmetry with one quark carrying more momentum than the other, whereas the $ho$ and $\phi$ (representing $D^*_s$) amplitudes are symmetric with momenta evenly distributed between the quarks. The calculated branching ratios for the $B 	o \pi(770) \gamma$, $B 	o D^*_s \gamma$, and $B_s 	o \phi(959) \gamma$ decays are found to be in agreement with experimental data.
